From: MahanHD <mahanheidari2003@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dma-direct: let ARM allocate buffers without a kernel mapping

dma_direct_alloc() hands DMA_ATTR_NO_KERNEL_MAPPING requests to
dma_direct_alloc_no_mapping() before it looks at the architecture, so on
32-bit ARM non-coherent devices bypass arch_dma_alloc() for them. That path
relies on arch_dma_prep_coherent() to clean the buffer from the cache and
ARM has none: the buffer comes back neither zeroed nor cleaned, dirty lines
can later be written back over what the device stored, and the memory's old
contents reach userspace through mmap. ARM's own allocator handles the
attribute (want_vaddr) and zeroes and flushes the pages, highmem included.

Take the shortcut only when the architecture has no allocator of its own or
the device is coherent, and free the same way.

Needed by 0115, whose camera buffers have no kernel mapping; the msm
carveout (msm.vram) is the other user here.

--- a/kernel/dma/direct.c
+++ b/kernel/dma/direct.c
@@ -205,6 +205,20 @@
 	return page;
 }
 
+/*
+ * Non-coherent devices on an architecture with its own allocator (32-bit
+ * ARM) get all their coherent buffers from it, those without a kernel
+ * mapping too: dma_direct_alloc_no_mapping() neither zeroes the buffer nor
+ * cleans it from the cache there (ARM has no arch_dma_prep_coherent()), so
+ * dirty lines could later be written back over what the device stored, and
+ * whatever the memory last held would reach userspace through mmap.
+ */
+static bool dma_direct_use_arch_alloc(struct device *dev)
+{
+	return IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_ARCH_HAS_DMA_ALLOC) &&
+	       !dev_is_dma_coherent(dev) && !is_swiotlb_for_alloc(dev);
+}
+
 void *dma_direct_alloc(struct device *dev, size_t size,
 		dma_addr_t *dma_handle, gfp_t gfp, unsigned long attrs)
 {
@@ -217,6 +231,7 @@
 		gfp |= __GFP_NOWARN;
 
 	if ((attrs & DMA_ATTR_NO_KERNEL_MAPPING) &&
+	    !dma_direct_use_arch_alloc(dev) &&
 	    !force_dma_unencrypted(dev) && !is_swiotlb_for_alloc(dev))
 		return dma_direct_alloc_no_mapping(dev, size, dma_handle, gfp);
 
@@ -318,6 +333,7 @@
 	unsigned int page_order = get_order(size);
 
 	if ((attrs & DMA_ATTR_NO_KERNEL_MAPPING) &&
+	    !dma_direct_use_arch_alloc(dev) &&
 	    !force_dma_unencrypted(dev) && !is_swiotlb_for_alloc(dev)) {
 		/* cpu_addr is a struct page cookie, not a kernel address */
 		dma_free_contiguous(dev, cpu_addr, size);
